## Proposed Architecture & Changes

### 1. Backend Server Layer

#### [MODIFY] [server/package.json](file:///c:/Users/Ashwin/Desktop/LMS/server/package.json)
- Add lightweight, pure JS extraction libraries:
  - `mammoth`: Fast, pure-JS `.docx` document extractor.
  - `pdf-parse`: Pure-JS PDF text extractor.

#### [NEW] [server/src/utils/documentScanner.js](file:///c:/Users/Ashwin/Desktop/LMS/server/src/utils/documentScanner.js)
- 4-Stage Security Verification:
  1. Magic Byte Signature Validation (`%PDF-`, PKZip for `.docx`).
  2. PDF Exploit Scan: Detects and rejects `/JavaScript`, `/JS`, `/Launch`, `/EmbeddedFiles`, `/OpenAction`.
  3. DOCX Threat Scan: Checks for VBA Macros (`vbaProject.bin`), DDE payloads, and disables external entity expansion (XXE).
  4. Text Sanitizer: Neutralizes `<script>`, `<iframe>`, and prompt injection attacks.

#### [NEW] [server/src/utils/questionExtractor.js](file:///c:/Users/Ashwin/Desktop/LMS/server/src/utils/questionExtractor.js)
- Universal parser that normalizes:
  - AI-generated Markdown (bolded questions, list bullets, etc.).
  - Hand-typed human documents (inconsistent delimiters like `1.`, `Q1:`, `1)`).
  - Web-downloaded exam papers with consolidated end-of-file answer keys.
- Outputs structured `{ questionText, options: [A, B, C, D], correctOption: 0..3, explanation }`.

#### [MODIFY] [server/src/controllers/assessmentController.js](file:///c:/Users/Ashwin/Desktop/LMS/server/src/controllers/assessmentController.js)
- Add secure upload & extraction endpoint (`POST /api/assessments/extract`).
- Add endpoint to save section/final exam assessments (`POST /api/assessments`).
- Update student take endpoint (`GET /api/assessments/:id/take`) with question sampling and strict payload sanitization (strip `correctOption` and `explanation`).
- Add grading logic (`POST /api/assessments/:id/submit`) comparing against session questions and pass threshold.

